; atc_measure.ngc — Tool length measurement against fixed G59.3 toolsetter
;
; Part of the flexiHAL ATC plugin.  Called by the C plugin after a tool is
; physically clamped in the spindle — either by the carousel (atc_change.ngc)
; or manually by the operator.  Also invoked directly by $TCMEASURE.
;
; PREREQUISITES
;   - Machine fully homed (XYZ)
;   - Spindle stopped, coolant off
;   - Tool clamped in spindle
;   - NGC expression support enabled in config (required for PRM[] and #5xxx)
;
; SETTINGS READ VIA PRM[]   (no caller parameters required)
;   $342  probing distance   mm        max downward travel toward toolsetter
;   $343  locate feed rate   mm/min    slow, accurate second probe
;   $344  seek feed rate     mm/min    fast first probe
;   $345  pulloff rate       mm/min    retract between fast and slow probes
;
; COORDINATE SYSTEM
;   G59.3 must be configured with:
;     X, Y  —  toolsetter centre (machine coordinates)
;     Z     —  approach height: top of toolsetter body + small air gap
;               (machine coordinate, i.e. a negative number on typical machines)
;   Parameters used: #5381 (G59.3 X), #5382 (G59.3 Y), #5383 (G59.3 Z)
;
; TOOL LENGTH OFFSET
;   Uses G10 L11 to store the measured length in the tool table.
;   G10 L11 sets the tool table entry so that — when G43 is subsequently
;   active and the machine is in G59.3 — the current position reads as the
;   given value.  Passing Z0 means "the tool tip is at the G59.3 Z origin",
;   which is the toolsetter trigger point.  grblHAL/LinuxCNC then back-calculates
;   and stores the correct absolute gauge length automatically.
;
;   G49 is issued before probing to cancel any active TLO so that the probe
;   result is a raw machine coordinate unaffected by a previous tool's offset.
;
;   After storing, G43 H#5400 reloads the offset for the current tool from
;   the table and activates it.  Subsequent motion is now compensated.
;
;   This approach:
;     - requires no reference tool or session-relative arithmetic
;     - stores an absolute gauge length that survives power cycles
;     - is consistent with the LinuxCNC G43 / G10 L11 definition
;
; SKIPPING ALREADY-PROBED TOOLS
;   If the tool table already contains a non-zero Z offset for the current
;   tool, the probe sequence is skipped and the stored offset is activated
;   directly via G43 H#5400.  This avoids unnecessary toolsetter cycles when
;   the carousel returns a tool that was measured in a previous session.
;
;   A zero Z offset means the tool has never been probed (or was explicitly
;   cleared by tc_reprobe_tool() to force re-measurement).  No real spindle
;   tool has a true zero gauge length, so zero is safe to use as a sentinel.
;
;   The C caller (tc_probe_tool / tc_manual_tool_change) ensures the tool
;   always has a table entry before this macro runs via tooltable_register_tool(),
;   so G65 P2 will always find a valid entry rather than erroring.
;
;   G65 P2 Q<tool> R<axis> reads the tool table Z offset into #<_value>.
;   Axis index 2 = Z.
;
; PROBE SEQUENCE
;   1.  Validate current tool number — abort if T0
;   2.  Read stored Z offset — skip to step 10 if non-zero (already measured)
;   3.  Cancel active TLO (G49)
;   4.  Rapid Z to home (G53 Z0)
;   5.  Rapid XY to G59.3 toolsetter position
;   6.  Rapid Z to G59.3 approach height
;   7.  Fast seek probe downward — G38.3 (no-error variant) at $344
;   8.  Abort with message if toolsetter was not triggered (#5070)
;   9.  Retract ($342 / 10) mm at $345
;   10. Slow locate probe — G38.2 (error-on-miss) at $343
;   11. Store gauge length: G10 L11 P#5400 Z0
;   12. Activate offset: G43 H#5400
;   13. Rapid Z to home

; ── 1. Validate tool number ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
; #5400 == 0 means no tool is selected — abort with a clear message.
; The C caller guarantees this won't happen in normal use, but guard anyway.
o100 if [#5400 EQ 0]
  (abort, ATC measure: no tool selected -- issue Tn M6 before measuring)
o100 endif

; ── 2. Check for existing offset — skip probe if already measured ─────────────
; G65 P2 Q<tool> R2 reads the Z offset for the tool into #<_value>.
; The C caller ensures the tool has a table entry before this macro runs,
; so this call is always valid (will not error with "undefined tool").
; tc_reprobe_tool() zeroes the entry via set_tool() to defeat this guard.
G65 P2 Q#5400 R2
o110 if [#<_value> NE 0]
  (print, ATC: tool #5400 already measured -- activating stored offset)
  G43 H#5400
  M2
o110 endif

; ── 3. Cancel active TLO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
G49

; ── 4. Safe Z — machine home ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
G53 G0 Z0

; ── 5. XY to toolsetter centre ───────────────────────────────────────────────
; #5381/#5382 are the G59.3 X and Y offsets (machine coordinates, persistent).
G53 G0 X#5381 Y#5382

; ── 6. Z to approach height ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
; #5383 is the G59.3 Z offset — the approach height above the toolsetter tip.
G53 G0 Z#5383

; ── 7. Fast seek — G38.3 (probe toward, no error on miss) ────────────────────
; PRM[344] = $344 seek rate.   PRM[342] = $342 probing distance.
G38.3 Z[#5383 - PRM[342]] F[PRM[344]]

; ── 8. Abort if toolsetter not triggered ─────────────────────────────────────
; #5070 = 1 when the last G38 probe cycle triggered, 0 if it did not.
o120 if [#5070 NE 1]
  (abort, ATC measure: toolsetter not triggered on seek -- check $342 and G59.3 Z)
o120 endif

; ── 9. Retract before slow probe ─────────────────────────────────────────────
G91
G1 Z[PRM[342] / 10] F[PRM[345]]
G90

; ── 10. Slow locate probe — G38.2 (probe toward, error on miss) ──────────────
G38.2 Z[#5383 - PRM[342]] F[PRM[343]]

; ── 11. Store gauge length in tool table ─────────────────────────────────────
; Z0 means "tool tip is at the G59.3 Z origin" — grblHAL back-calculates the
; absolute gauge length and stores it persistently in the tool table file.
G10 L11 P#5400 Z0

; ── 12. Activate tool length offset ──────────────────────────────────────────
G43 H#5400

(print, ATC: tool #5400 measured and stored)

; ── 13. Retract to home Z ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
G53 G0 Z0

M2
